## SECTION 6: Recommended Enterprise Architecture

### 6.1 Authentication & Authorization Layer

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[User Login] --> B[Supabase Auth]
    B --> C{JWT Token}
    C --> D[Custom Claims: role, org_id, permissions]
    D --> E[RLS Policies on Every Table]
    D --> F[Client-Side Route Guards]
    D --> G[Edge Function Auth Middleware]
```

**Requirements:**
1. Store role in `app_metadata` (server-only, not client-writable) via a Supabase trigger on profile creation
2. Implement `PrivateRoute` component wrapping all authenticated routes
3. Create RLS policies for every table based on `auth.jwt() -> app_metadata -> role`
4. Remove all hardcoded API tokens from client code — proxy AI calls through edge functions

### 6.2 Database Architecture (Normalized)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    organizations ||--o{ departments : has
    departments ||--o{ teams : has
    teams ||--o{ employees : contains
    
    employees ||--|| profiles : "is a"
    employees ||--o{ payroll_records : receives
    employees ||--o{ leave_requests : submits
    employees ||--o{ performance_reviews : has
    employees ||--o{ work_sessions : logs
    
    job_requisitions ||--o{ job_postings : creates
    job_postings ||--o{ applications : receives
    applications ||--|| candidates : "from"
    applications ||--o{ assessment_assignments : triggers
    applications ||--o{ interview_rounds : schedules
    applications ||--o| offer_letters : generates
    
    candidates ||--o{ documents : uploads
    documents ||--o{ verifications : undergoes
    
    offer_letters ||--o| onboarding_records : initiates
    onboarding_records ||--|| employees : creates
```

### 6.3 Service Layer Architecture

Instead of direct Supabase calls in every component:

```
Component → Custom Hook → Service Layer → Supabase Client
                              ↓
                        Error Handling
                        Type Validation
                        Audit Logging
                        Cache Management
```

### 6.4 AI Integration Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    A[Client Request] --> B[Edge Function Proxy]
    B --> C{Rate Limiter}
    C --> D[Token Management - Server Side]
    D --> E[HuggingFace / OpenAI]
    E --> F[Response Sanitization]
    F --> G[Structured JSON Validation]
    G --> H[Database Persistence]
    H --> I[Client Response]
```

All AI calls must be routed through Supabase Edge Functions to:
- Keep API tokens server-side
- Enforce rate limiting per user/role
- Validate and sanitize AI outputs
- Log all AI decisions for audit compliance

